---
layout: base.njk
permalink: /services.html
fullTitle: "Pitch Coaching & Workshops Perth | 1:1 Sessions from $59 | Take the Leap"
description: "Book a 30, 60 or 90-minute session with Victoria Howe for help with your pitch, presentation, messaging or marketing. Plus hands-on pitch masterclasses for accelerators and founder programs."
ctaText: "Not sure which session you need? Book 30 minutes and we'll work it out together."
---
<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">1:1 sessions · Masterclasses · Workshops</span>
    <h1>Bring what you're <em>stuck on.</em></h1>
    <p class="lede">No packages, no retainer, no long onboarding. Book focused, practical time on your pitch, your message or your marketing, sized to what you need right now.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section tight" id="book" style="padding-top:0">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="book-grid">
      {%- for s in booking.sessions %}
      <article class="book-card{% if s.id == '60' %} pop{% endif %}">
        <span class="len">{{ s.length }} · {{ s.name }}</span>
        <span class="price">{{ s.price }}</span>
        <p>{{ s.blurb }}</p>
        <a class="btn {% if s.id == '60' %}btn-solid{% else %}btn-line{% endif %}" href="{{ s.url }}">Choose a time</a>
      </article>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
    <p class="evening-note" style="margin-top:22px">{{ booking.evening }}</p>
    <ol class="how" aria-label="How booking works">
      <li><div><h3>Pick a time</h3><p>Choose a session length and a time that suits you in my calendar.</p></div></li>
      <li><div><h3>Get your invoice</h3><p>I'll send you an invoice to lock in your spot.</p></div></li>
      <li><div><h3>Get to work</h3><p>Bring your pitch, deck or problem. Leave with a clear next step.</p></div></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section blush">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">What we can work on</span>
      <h2>If it involves being understood, bring it</h2>
    </div>
    <ul class="chips">
      <li>Investor pitches</li>
      <li>Pitch decks</li>
      <li>Grant applications</li>
      <li>Presentations</li>
      <li>Pitch nights &amp; showcases</li>
      <li>Messaging</li>
      <li>Marketing</li>
      <li>Social media guidance</li>
      <li>Confidence &amp; delivery</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="outcomes">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">What you walk away with</span>
      <h2>Something done, not just discussed</h2>
    </div>
    <ul class="outcomes">
      <li><h3>A pitch you can deliver</h3><p>Tightened and rehearsed, so investors or customers get the point in the first thirty seconds.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Clarity on your message</h3><p>A simple way to explain what you do and why it matters. The version that works in a lift, not just in a deck.</p></li>
      <li><h3>A presentation that's ready</h3><p>Slides and delivery worked through together, so you walk in knowing exactly what you'll say.</p></li>
      <li><h3>A marketing next step</h3><p>A practical move for your marketing or social media, not a 40-page strategy you'll never open.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Confidence under pressure</h3><p>Tools for staying composed and clear at a pitch competition, in a hard conversation or in front of investors.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Something built</h3><p>In longer sessions we make the thing together: a graphic, a one-pager, a post. You leave with it.</p></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section dark on-dark" id="workshops">
  <div class="wrap split" style="align-items:start">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">For sprints, accelerators &amp; teams</span>
      <h2 class="display" style="font-size:clamp(36px,4.6vw,60px);margin-block:14px 20px">Pitch masterclasses founders actually use</h2>
      <p style="color:var(--on-dark-soft);font-size:18px;max-width:34em">A hands-on session, usually two hours, tailored to your cohort's stage. Founders don't just listen. They write their pitch, stand up, deliver it and get feedback in the room.</p>
      <p style="color:var(--on-dark-soft);font-size:18px;max-width:34em;margin-top:14px">Currently running in Plus Eight sprint and accelerator programs, including the City of Joondalup Pre-Accelerator. Also delivered for Innovation Shed, where I'm now a mentor.</p>
      <div class="cta-row" style="margin-top:28px">
        <a class="btn btn-solid" href="/contact?topic=workshop">Enquire about a masterclass</a>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top:14px;font-size:14px;color:#CBB7C8">Pricing on application</p>
      <figure class="photo" style="margin-top:32px">
        <img src="/images/plus-eight-joondalup.jpg" alt="Victoria with the Plus Eight City of Joondalup Pre-Accelerator team in front of a Congratulations slide" width="1400" height="1050" loading="lazy">
        <figcaption style="color:#CBB7C8">Plus Eight City of Joondalup Pre-Accelerator program</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <div>
      <ul class="path" aria-label="What a masterclass covers" style="border-color:var(--pink-light)">
        <li><h3 style="color:#fff">Why pitching matters</h3><p style="color:var(--on-dark-soft)">You pitch more often than you think: investors, customers, partners, hires.</p></li>
        <li><h3 style="color:#fff">What makes a pitch compelling</h3><p style="color:var(--on-dark-soft)">Clear, simple, focused, a story, energy, and something people can repeat.</p></li>
        <li><h3 style="color:#fff">The framework</h3><p style="color:var(--on-dark-soft)">Hook, problem, shift, solution, proof, ask, pressure test. Plus a one-page worksheet.</p></li>
        <li><h3 style="color:#fff">The 10-second conversation starter</h3><p style="color:var(--on-dark-soft)">For networking and chance meetings. Everyone writes theirs on the spot.</p></li>
        <li><h3 style="color:#fff">Presenting with confidence</h3><p style="color:var(--on-dark-soft)">Eye contact, hands, pace, pauses and handling the room.</p></li>
        <li><h3 style="color:#fff">Live pitches and feedback</h3><p style="color:var(--on-dark-soft)">Three minutes each, with feedback on clarity, structure and confidence.</p></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% include "cta.njk" %}
